{"title":"2026 Bespoked Osaka Picks 03: Aya, Blue Lug, Cook Paint Works, Cicli Barco – John Watson","link":"https://theradavist.com/2026-bespoked-osaka-picks-03","date":1793169000000,"content":"<p><em>Maido from Osaka! Cari and John were in attendance at the <a href=\"https://theradavist.com/tag/2026-bespoked-osaka\" target=\"_blank\">2026 Bespoked Osaka</a> event, where they documented a variety of bikes from the global framebuilding community. Read on for a look at the Bespoked Osaka venue and a selection of builders including Aya Bikes, Blue Lug, Cook Paint Works, and Cicli Barco…</em><span></span></p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/9e0028a37fef25d3ad320b2c512b2e9578f6e9b3ed3ae02f420a0176cd5966fa.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/a4263a1395143a9783b28cabf2c8b4dcae115437daf16322461d224f920332b8.jpg 640w, /media/9e0028a37fef25d3ad320b2c512b2e9578f6e9b3ed3ae02f420a0176cd5966fa.jpg 1800w, /media/de3e0dfba7ea345b9d528f2994a4ca1eec3db60788b9ebe28dee377668ce07ea.jpg\" /></p>\n<h3><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/aya_bikes/?hl=en\" target=\"_blank\">Aya Bikes</a> Ghooost ATB</h3>\n<p>Himeji City-based Aya Akamatsu learned to build frames at the Tokyo College of Cycle Design; three years later, she began building the Sim Works Doppo frames for four years. At the 2026 Bespoked Osaka event, she unveiled Mai Ohara from Ghooost’s new bike.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/dad25e8954c151c1fb2b11b1c6f68b9eeffb877c71d41b2107c6bd2770a232c9.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/b1ca66232d8704bbac463dfe9a19ce67fb559d861e14b2d0e21f2db5271e29e8.jpg 800w, /media/dad25e8954c151c1fb2b11b1c6f68b9eeffb877c71d41b2107c6bd2770a232c9.jpg 1600w, /media/c3d519e81db9076a08992e54979075c8b20d272cfe9f2e8c43d28842b06f0f90.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/72f54dd9be6e8d08307d3557f57a8029ddc49ada1a23b9834f9a4978fcb8f33a.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/be8a5a865a7bb4b52f6a16547585291c3a0296375fb9a7b51a69b42b6c99412c.jpg 800w, /media/72f54dd9be6e8d08307d3557f57a8029ddc49ada1a23b9834f9a4978fcb8f33a.jpg 1600w, /media/719ce48812cd989e5d4b4adfcd268304136914959275ce8f24701311ef826cde.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/77f8e9bb2a48aeadfc5861f608cf812d23859264478de5c513c369f969e19fe4.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/a1a683771f4cb661ee41b66407ef2e092da9b1f53d7104dd0484ae092cb3b2fb.jpg 800w, /media/77f8e9bb2a48aeadfc5861f608cf812d23859264478de5c513c369f969e19fe4.jpg 1600w, /media/64198d5081969a1acaa52130ca6b5195b8f090579ac69bed2b1df61855968212.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>Aya wanted to make a frame for shorter Japanese people, particularly women, and Mai was the perfect client for this first bike. The average ATB or gravel bike on the market is often too big for Japanese women, so Aya worked on perfecting the size and proportions of the frame for Mai. Some beautiful details are found throughout, including reinforcement rings of brass, which are perforated with small holes that were inspired by Mai’s artwork.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/333502665cc8bbfff8473ab6e03d45efa08d8bc012be696964ed08baf46f8350.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/eda279faebe0494151c30be8c5db8249f64a72e5ed957a94d28838aad06e8ce2.jpg 800w, /media/333502665cc8bbfff8473ab6e03d45efa08d8bc012be696964ed08baf46f8350.jpg 1600w, /media/4bfabebd16ff1e4f5725c7583f00fc43c30106d54b83760ad4142823126b8eaf.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/83e386c05adb0e49de9eae69380c3b97e182a0bc5079752944b982884e4f96a1.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/a2f04d4e90f031b74a8cc76c36788d93fe00c81e7fb34de2ab57563ebf80377b.jpg 800w, /media/83e386c05adb0e49de9eae69380c3b97e182a0bc5079752944b982884e4f96a1.jpg 1600w, /media/c7e10e5ac5719a1c2edf81e43751a7067b60a7fef3fe351077ab933b5380c8fa.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/d2f8103c198a4d803eaf8e04f32e88b0ea8cfc91df44296f64527c14dd3ec73e.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/315a611bc19c41e3f436731ce091c8f921610e2cd5840eaf0c9fe831cadea850.jpg 800w, /media/d2f8103c198a4d803eaf8e04f32e88b0ea8cfc91df44296f64527c14dd3ec73e.jpg 1600w, /media/76604bcebae2601c44ae14b46fccf880f262af540d312f9d6604fc22f3044be5.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>Once the frame was complete, Aya had one last thing to do: build a stem for it. After that, the bike was complete. For the Bespoked show, Mai put on the finishing touches with her playful illustrations and creatures, including a special note for <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/jonnypucci/?hl=en\" target=\"_blank\">Jonny Pucci</a> to come paint the bike in Japan.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/751932c39967a97db065dd347a5ce85a1cac968843836a75541e2c52c2b2b253.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/f73192787e7fe56a9df29c92ac85610e9fa1465334f6b7cac00373e4729c2e99.jpg 640w, /media/751932c39967a97db065dd347a5ce85a1cac968843836a75541e2c52c2b2b253.jpg 1800w, /media/48c3ca2b2e2e2db35410924e74744cc07f8362d82e020becb39fefd59ee871f5.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>Mai, Aya, and their friend V, an English interpreter, were super busy all weekend at Bespoked. We’re big fans of Ghooost over here and can’t wait to see Mai ride this bike all over the globe.</p>\n<h3><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/aya_bikes/?hl=en\" target=\"_blank\">@AyaBikes</a></h3>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/19e7868b1c5091a2d7d80b605e87a06f5e13a70749e840f381effab6264f38f8.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/ef9a4db650862ff3d2f441e3fa16c4f3da63762df08e5fd3a1dc1ec65610d116.jpg 640w, /media/19e7868b1c5091a2d7d80b605e87a06f5e13a70749e840f381effab6264f38f8.jpg 1800w, /media/9707b4870163a8cd8ad74fe20cb65d4124d40f44bd3116e41086be45fd6d2979.jpg\" /></p>\n<h3><a href=\"https://bluelug.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blue Lug</a> x Toyo x Falconer Pro Cruiser Homage “Chukar”</h3>\n<p>Walking into one of the two Bespoked Osaka halls, my vintage MTB-loving eyes were immediately drawn to this Pro Cruiser homage on display at the Blue Lug booth. Little did I know that Cameron Falconer – who has actually stepped aside from his framebuilding business recently – didn’t actually build the bike. Rather, when Tani from Blue Lug approached Cam to build a frame, he gladly handed over the drawings to Japanese builder Mr. Ishigaki from Toyo.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/1222966c5e870cb5b545cf98879544688b58fcb26b407b7bbc922ec9575f0473.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/296edade136c686cddde94f974e7ab289c6be12f4a6d3396ff65b42a475746e9.jpg 800w, /media/d77ea7c8caa3a55ca40cbb557a1cc3f88d3b440fa802690700890b483c60be1d.jpg 1600w, /media/1222966c5e870cb5b545cf98879544688b58fcb26b407b7bbc922ec9575f0473.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/66e618cb82abd1fcb69a0ae2f6e3ad6991e21fa5e3db9a3f671f19f49477fa42.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/19817ee74a5be8d1f2c5f4e1fe1e2e4743b29c70cc3aef5b2300d261edb76340.jpg 800w, /media/b04ee4ca33fb76cfdccc098f5c2e6092de85cd851f7890fcac01ca3931b7d5a9.jpg 1600w, /media/66e618cb82abd1fcb69a0ae2f6e3ad6991e21fa5e3db9a3f671f19f49477fa42.jpg\" /></p>\n<p><em>Left, Mr. Ishigaki </em><em>is shown with a special Japan-built Rivendell he also made for Blue Lug for a small batch coming out in 2027… Champion BMX downtube piercing, right.</em></p>\n<p>Toyo has been building bikes since the 1980s and was actually one of the first Japanese builders to make mountain bikes for various brands, including the first Specialized Stumpjumpers. After Mike Sinyard from Specialized bought a Ritchey frame and shipped it to Japan to be copied, Toyo delivered the brand’s first mountain bike.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/a6ecd15b078d1520bb9f79621abce3fcbfe97661f24285b53cc3b5c822e016f0.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/7998b3342c01c8a3df93cd8e3c064ab91c5b92d285303ba7617ebb907e1bd372.jpg 800w, /media/a6ecd15b078d1520bb9f79621abce3fcbfe97661f24285b53cc3b5c822e016f0.jpg 1600w, /media/90f3e7c0df739be6eb3576c779880555bf923c7adabda5513e3a3bb072cccb99.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/41568c4213b6458903bf15bf5ce162909162a4dd7db02f90143c9dc913e24a93.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/3f7f3529d4e4002ff37c4fd02a511681e6c7022dcce0291c825bc50d962f5cdb.jpg 800w, /media/41568c4213b6458903bf15bf5ce162909162a4dd7db02f90143c9dc913e24a93.jpg 1600w, /media/26ceeb6674b80326a48f9d78f2859756cadcf3187e0f50d5609a69e077a6e2f2.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/2db907132e6165df92e25728511f40a25c0109d9623cf8ae63d93555e04197a7.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/23494d34a66ce9e9cee5c8dc3ecd9d5cb8c8f40d27cf169a84e9439119e6da42.jpg 800w, /media/2db907132e6165df92e25728511f40a25c0109d9623cf8ae63d93555e04197a7.jpg 1600w, /media/d11e3f05d2ae68954f4df1e8f497ec30f779fa657545e542104e310e5af8ee70.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>Needless to say, Toyo was the perfect company to build this bike. He even went as far as to pierce the downtube with the diagatube, just as Champion BMX had done so in the original design the Pro Cruiser was inspired by.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/2186d3226e8ff5833ce2dbf65f5f33c2ce7e934b725e23ebbdaae1c9b2cc1e68.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/f4e5dd413383f8fe66b9c2c61c747257d1e6779078d8d093a79d1d625dd349eb.jpg 640w, /media/2186d3226e8ff5833ce2dbf65f5f33c2ce7e934b725e23ebbdaae1c9b2cc1e68.jpg 1800w, /media/480b0b822d4ca620cb6548e189389ac013226d5d3445cd0cfd73246bf86272ea.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>Blue Lug will be producing these bikes in a small batch next year, and I cannot wait. To the whole team at Blue Lug. Thank you!</p>\n<h3><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/bluelug/?hl=en\" target=\"_blank\">@BlueLug</a></h3>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/8bc4190833d0625fd089cc8d343e01b3c31cbd91dd5408000c78a488f1facca3.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/952b7bcec24eaf789a6dc6f7a2c2b15906214cdce6686c7fe554e1c33faf8dc4.jpg 640w, /media/8bc4190833d0625fd089cc8d343e01b3c31cbd91dd5408000c78a488f1facca3.jpg 1800w, /media/64249c6e0fcd1e6a9c0427a921ab60ab117afd44d1a2f36406eceea9f6ab8cd8.jpg\" /></p>\n<h3><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/cookpaintworks/?hl=en\" target=\"_blank\">Cook Paint Works</a> x <a href=\"https://ronsbikes.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Ron’s Bikes</a></h3>\n<p>Blue Lug’s in-house paint shop, Cook Paint Works, <a href=\"https://theradavist.com/cicli-pucci-for-blue-lug-rons-bikes\" target=\"_blank\">recently collaborated with San Diego artist and bicycle painter Jonny Pucci</a> on a limited run of Ron’s Bikes frames. We reported on that collaboration earlier this year. Following that momentum, Konno-boy from Cook looked around the Blue Lug shop at various sewn goods for inspiration to paint two more frames.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/5cf1e6fd7e9199af7f314804814dc1a277821891597a1c26ffc8a752e16163e6.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/361d3c65e9d501749efe7ffc8c1041067c2e670c7745d3fbebd78fe723347f1c.jpg 800w, /media/c8058f4b5d319578a7cf9fcf2dc02c1f3a78e51fc698e4e18d3c8f7891ff2941.jpg 1600w, /media/5cf1e6fd7e9199af7f314804814dc1a277821891597a1c26ffc8a752e16163e6.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/331b11779da89ee548d5b5d5cda92107784932aa9327522b4a1e82b513f0f4a2.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/d3f46984b287ca59b4015f6586d3fadc874235edb794307d6e8511b1de003cd1.jpg 800w, /media/c82fd83d459c6370dc63ea8fa340c4b155bc7f6b37c4f46841f553a49998c7e4.jpg 1600w, /media/331b11779da89ee548d5b5d5cda92107784932aa9327522b4a1e82b513f0f4a2.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>The Darren Larkin-built <a href=\"https://ronsbikes.com/products/mid-reach-road-bike\" target=\"_blank\">steel CR1</a> long-reach caliper road bike was painted to resemble a tie-dye seat cushion Konno uses while working, while the Frank the Welder-built <a href=\"https://ronsbikes.com/products/aluminus-maximus\" target=\"_blank\">Alumax II</a> was painted with a “Night Tree Camo” pattern—a design featured on the Shtak messenger bags made by Jag that Konno uses.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/9ac8e923d79b4683bbfb09d25ac4120fc004ac7aeefeb4174f3113e50294bf81.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/36d3ae7430c5f632b25325bc9534588003686d442bc76cd7dad081ca6a2f8acd.jpg 800w, /media/9ac8e923d79b4683bbfb09d25ac4120fc004ac7aeefeb4174f3113e50294bf81.jpg 1600w, /media/4cc7fdf03a8cded82439355a01beda20bc4c1c64de64b87a9ba78c63ec2f0344.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/366aadb8c9e74d4334b04eadcd8cd9bd5eea14d6b445b9f2225117603b8d84bb.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/8074d4ee24fc05900c378256894f4d9c245d85cc0f449bf4f7880b38c7969e3d.jpg 800w, /media/366aadb8c9e74d4334b04eadcd8cd9bd5eea14d6b445b9f2225117603b8d84bb.jpg 1600w, /media/44c514d1bcb678c59a29a5ff55599b1b856875df503ff0c56c7cd45fe559e3b3.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/ab6f253887e0153f92fa068c38fac7c1495ea0074ca026b79d7dc9b28a0a22d5.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/338abd26f8170571fed67a7d1674ff929090c2735abb364111b1f19115658756.jpg 800w, /media/ab6f253887e0153f92fa068c38fac7c1495ea0074ca026b79d7dc9b28a0a22d5.jpg 1600w, /media/35043c60eef6941fc20a7b46c6aa80d6c4e8aba9b0e703eaf1ba0c3729d3e717.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>The Cook logo on the Alumax II was made with gold leafing, a special touch Konno will add to his most favorite projects, upping the ante for the Bespoked Osaka showcase.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/49df28c002fc93425c54a790a4ad499541646e98b06f0d53763034acbdfadcdd.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/ff1897f574c72ca0fcbed333296635b13292b95a585b353aeed001fedf9ab5fb.jpg 800w, /media/9b0ac479743e0b1722a796a74f6ce24a7a267f1fac47257bbefe680439789319.jpg 1600w, /media/49df28c002fc93425c54a790a4ad499541646e98b06f0d53763034acbdfadcdd.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/6c4f9c0ab95f4fc6e145f0c2fd5dc3f5aa735ee331bf2a0e8181ce45a3ed92d6.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/8c1b90adc5f93b0b8521ccd6cd7130927e4946af608578f2e738891c02a0f3c8.jpg 800w, /media/cc2595e51159964434c82586b68fbe83396c473f963397420e5529e4bbb5592a.jpg 1600w, /media/6c4f9c0ab95f4fc6e145f0c2fd5dc3f5aa735ee331bf2a0e8181ce45a3ed92d6.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>To the entire Blue Lug crew, arigato gozaimasu!</p>\n<h3><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/cookpaintworks/?hl=en\" target=\"_blank\">@CookPaintWorks</a> <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/ronsbikes/?hl=en\" target=\"_blank\">@RonsBikes</a></h3>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/b2579e324fa11196234cd53c9d79c8c08030a8a21679713d2c763b0d0d179c9d.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/a0e403340db0f2cfc5e365f98a2453e0e33f45d810a63029e171e49e0d00258c.jpg 640w, /media/b2579e324fa11196234cd53c9d79c8c08030a8a21679713d2c763b0d0d179c9d.jpg 1800w, /media/105f60aad38f8d408f7207c6c075a842dc9dda9909b09c7df5aaca62002c792a.jpg\" /></p>\n<h3><a href=\"https://www.ciclibarco.it/\" target=\"_blank\">Cicli Barco</a> Viva Integrated Disc Road</h3>\n<p>Fitting hydraulic brake lines into a 1 1/8″ cockpit was no easy task for Piazzola sul Brenta, Italy-based Cicli Barco. The Italian builder dropped the mic on modern steel road bikes using obtuse carbon forks for integrated cockpits, proving it is, in fact, a certain possibility for more traditional lines and proportions.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/c0738760203c0af3b77d80dac0111cb47db4bf94383383a52ba2c55d07667e19.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/1692ec90d6a01387559ae6193fe2abce4e55b4c88b73c40839cc25a436f6f267.jpg 800w, /media/c0738760203c0af3b77d80dac0111cb47db4bf94383383a52ba2c55d07667e19.jpg 1600w, /media/b42ef9bb0a49a4a827860247c4c1c81e664dd79efde67adeea3cdc18c943afc6.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/70e3a4d8a78ae9def0542f48b35b3a5e09cfc19e76b854a1c49423e03b61e8f8.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/db3edc9004caf22f6a21184f1703b281de90bc3aa6cc8a47730009ae79ab2d74.jpg 800w, /media/70e3a4d8a78ae9def0542f48b35b3a5e09cfc19e76b854a1c49423e03b61e8f8.jpg 1600w, /media/60ee920d54feab12cdd46de61aadcc688fb0285f65bbff774c1b3c167aa6ae42.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/3d226297d823fc3fdac4c7aec5bb93c656d2107590b5cdbf317d38460fa4b051.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/cd0e8c2cbe4970b792e9a5f499e3c5e8d06affc59440c16f2cc2f6b02f56044e.jpg 800w, /media/3d226297d823fc3fdac4c7aec5bb93c656d2107590b5cdbf317d38460fa4b051.jpg 1600w, /media/dde09aa49a8c082d30d26869b9f1bc847b0db594225c2cc8ef0732b01d398d27.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>Gianluca Barco walked me through the process it took to cram brake hoses into the Ritchey bars, through the stem and into the head tube. When I requested photos of the spaghetti, he winced, noting that getting it all into the frame takes time and patience. Perhaps we’ll see more some other day.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/66825a41becec442d3688eb9c0665b9695f13dcaa4fce46590e9087601ae0cf2.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/ecb2cf267cafaf882b610ce2ec470bd664ebb5d4e49ca3089ddd69b33eac97e5.jpg 800w, /media/66825a41becec442d3688eb9c0665b9695f13dcaa4fce46590e9087601ae0cf2.jpg 1600w, /media/359ea03842afab97872d20ecdcb0513c7da6055b74dec62d15271c86f4445ec6.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/ed237a84437e567cc78f9ef4fbf206c81bb47713aeac96601fb284a045233508.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/93c8b9af22143baf2830fb4e987e42acfa1a97f74b738031ee0c2bcc6a232df5.jpg 800w, /media/ed237a84437e567cc78f9ef4fbf206c81bb47713aeac96601fb284a045233508.jpg 1600w, /media/f2cca27e6c70835e943274de070dcff656b359331dd8d698b963e3dbe141dfaf.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/441f4ec89dc17cf4e83488270c6a0ab6cdd407dbd0d4981d327fe1fc94d4814c.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/0f65127a4948c8be9c26377fe8c327e5f1c346e87c9ee2ba1568f0959746d253.jpg 800w, /media/441f4ec89dc17cf4e83488270c6a0ab6cdd407dbd0d4981d327fe1fc94d4814c.jpg 1600w, /media/c96e9002a85d5568609d244e6256e28f255f44c972103e6a9c55936621556f1f.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>This stainless steel beauty has nods to the Cicli Barco heritage as an Italian manufacturer for bigger brands throughout the decades. Featured throughout is a “B” from the Barco namesake, hidden on the underside of the stem, on the ends of the custom-made titanium thru-axles, dropouts, and bottom bracket.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/cbecc405ce0a5f021810975a4c489a2346ff5960778a1dc6ac6ad1608e93d5b3.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/f351e96d1c112b95d2ba7ced1fde83643e2737f01e5171a6b0ff61f97d022db3.jpg 800w, /media/cbecc405ce0a5f021810975a4c489a2346ff5960778a1dc6ac6ad1608e93d5b3.jpg 1600w, /media/8d3fb72adb997e9ade97b60e25c793823ed6c2bac38d93716185d54f437e5a9d.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/11416534a7ac616d35feebadaffe89e59cc741f697be81c44d19e45307e06040.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/5b9a4f1696f8596856251fa0f406cad67bfdb7326dbfca85631cfdf6d427e4ea.jpg 800w, /media/11416534a7ac616d35feebadaffe89e59cc741f697be81c44d19e45307e06040.jpg 1600w, /media/d7db34a0442a8fe79e864c83ca2956dbf9fddcf6a15bce05b23aad8a622ad872.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/816c6fa638056cb9e4e0d5877272542e276fd0067bd9c6bd6690f24995f9fd66.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/960d0b4f7d1a6c62af78258a38ffa2c4f2b6cb3c9d0e4b24d8ea1d6978b50074.jpg 800w, /media/816c6fa638056cb9e4e0d5877272542e276fd0067bd9c6bd6690f24995f9fd66.jpg 1600w, /media/7af03c2afbc8d38dc8733c0997fec5851617d6f2d851bb20bc574253ea596d1c.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>The stem’s compression slit is off-center; the fastback seat cluster uses titanium hardware, and the elegant stainless steel fork balances the proportions with an elegance only the Italians can showcase. This bike was hands down both Petor Georgallou, the Bespoked owner and director, and my own favorite road bike at the show. It embodies the blending of classic Italian heritage with modern demands, in a package that is both traditional and innovative.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/3667f79d063700c9e42dfb3cb320be285bead90fc54f249d8e12349276e914e1.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/c7277fcdf11157ba47d6d99f5153862abaad11fae0e01bfb839bd443339979ad.jpg 640w, /media/3667f79d063700c9e42dfb3cb320be285bead90fc54f249d8e12349276e914e1.jpg 1800w, /media/5855f47a8e85695a84f523b84a38177d131a756de467867746e5fd326b3b3e4d.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>Gianluca, it was a pleasure and an honor to document your work.</p>\n<h3><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/ciclibarco/?hl=en\" target=\"_blank\">@CicliBarco</a></h3>\n<p> </p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/f9fd5eea3c0bbb108d8df7a5414991806d8c0427188ae9a2c2b7679de681aeb5.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/9954310137f6738ee011aefc3c7c315dab21a4b533d1f5b27859b3e5032d4c21.jpg 640w, /media/f9fd5eea3c0bbb108d8df7a5414991806d8c0427188ae9a2c2b7679de681aeb5.jpg 1800w, /media/21b9972d77bdd0aa14d9f6047ffd04feaefb08e2579ae6221c6854d95f0e7f58.jpg\" /></p>\n<p><strong>The Radavist thanks <a href=\"https://circles-jp.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Circles Japan</a> for sponsoring our 2026 Bespoked Osaka coverage and our independent Reportage!</strong></p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://theradavist.com/2026-bespoked-osaka-picks-03\">2026 Bespoked Osaka Picks 03: Aya, Blue Lug, Cook Paint Works, Cicli Barco</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://cms.theradavist.com/\">The Radavist</a>.</p>","author":"John Watson","comments":"https://theradavist.com/2026-bespoked-osaka-picks-03#comments","siteTitle":"The Radavist","siteHash":"96eb481d8084f04a4602bac57874ba717baf56b758f45547b5caf2312da766ef","entryHash":"11477d0558908528a031dff1f74c2aa8d1fe05be0f2ea5a8062c02b17224db11","category":"Cycling"}